Article 1 The People's Court shall accept the following copyright civil dispute cases:
(1) cases involving disputes over ownership, infringement, or contract with respect to copyright and rights related to copyright;
(2) cases involving applications for pre-litigation cessation of acts infringing copyright or rights related to copyright, applications for pre-litigation property preservation, and pre-litigation evidence preservation;
(3) other cases involving disputes over copyright and rights related to copyright.

Article 4 A civil action brought for an act of copyright infringement shall be under the jurisdiction of the People's Court at the place where the infringing act provided in Articles 47 and 48 of the Copyright Law is committed, the place where infringing copies are stored, the place of sealing and seizure, or the place of the defendant's domicile.
The place where infringing copies are stored as referred to in the preceding paragraph means the place where infringing copies are stored or concealed in large quantities or on a regular basis;
the place of sealing and seizure means the place where the customs, copyright, and other administrative organs lawfully seal and seize infringing copies.

Article 11 For a dispute arising from the order of signature on a work, the People's Court shall handle it in accordance with the following principles:
if there is an agreement, the order of signature shall be determined according to the agreement;
if there is no agreement, the order may be determined based on the labor contributed to the creation of the work, the arrangement of the works, the number of strokes in the authors' surnames, and other factors.

Article 27 The limitation of action for infringement of copyright shall be three years, calculated from the date on which the copyright owner knows or should have known that the right was damaged and the identity of the obligor.
If the right holder brings a prosecution after more than three years, and the infringing act is still ongoing at the time of prosecution, the People's Court shall, within the term of protection of the copyright, adjudicate that the defendant cease the infringing act;
the amount of damages for infringement shall be calculated retroactively for three years from the date on which the right holder initiates the prosecution before the People's Court.

Article 29 Except as otherwise provided in this Interpretation, for copyright civil dispute cases accepted by the People's Court, if the civil acts involved occurred before the amendment of the Copyright Law, the provisions of the Copyright Law before the amendment shall apply;
if the civil acts occurred after the amendment of the Copyright Law, the provisions of the Copyright Law after the amendment shall apply;
if the civil acts occurred before the amendment of the Copyright Law and continued to after the amendment, the provisions of the Copyright Law after the amendment shall apply.
